    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d754">

                <pb facs="0714" n="616" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg616"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Choate to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1900-06-27"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 27, 1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 350.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 344, of the
                    20th instant, and to your telegram in reply, dated the 22d instant, both
                    relative to the terms of payment for Mr. Geldart’s shipment on the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Mashona</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Beatrice</hi>,
                    I have the honor to inclose herewith the copy of a note which I have addressed
                    to Lord Salisbury on the subject dated yesterday.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph H. Choate.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d754-a1.xml" xpointer="d754-a1"/>
